+Also called: NeurMiPs, Neural Mixture of Planar Experts, Neural Mixture of Planar Experts for View Synthesis
 
 ## Overview
-NeurMiPs represents a 3D scene as a mixture of $K$ learnable rectangular planar surfaces, where each surface acts as an independent "expert" predicting view-dependent color and transparency via a local neural radiance field [S1]. It alleviates the frontal-parallel limitation of traditional Multi-Plane Imagery (MPI) while maintaining high efficiency through analytical ray-plane intersection and parallel CUDA execution, offering superior extrapolation capabilities compared to voxel-based methods like PlenOctrees and KiloNeRF [S1].
+NeurMiPs is a view synthesis method that represents a 3D scene as a mixture of $K$ learnable rectangular planar surfaces, where each surface acts as an independent "expert" with an associated neural radiance field predicting view-dependent color and transparency [S1]. It alleviates the frontal-parallel limitation of traditional Multi-Plane Imagery (MPI) while maintaining high efficiency through closed-form ray-casting, offering better memory and computational efficiency than standard NeRF and superior extrapolation capabilities compared to voxel-based methods like PlenOctrees or KiloNeRF [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** Sparse 3D point cloud $\{x_i\}$ from Structure-from-Motion (SfM) [S1]; ground-truth images and camera poses [S1].
-**Outputs:** Rendered image color $c(r)$ for a ray $r$; depth map $d(r)$ [S1].
